Our fix for xas_pause() (lib/xarray.c), against the tree just before
upstream c9ba5249ef8b.  xas_pause() moves xa_index forward by
(offset - xa_offset) << shift, where offset is the first slot past the
current entry and its siblings.  But after a walk that starts inside a
multi-index entry, xa_index is neither aligned to node->shift (what
c9ba5249 fixed, by masking those bits) nor in the slot xa_offset names:
xas_descend() resolves a sibling slot to the entry's canonical slot, so
xa_offset is the canonical slot while xa_index still points at the
sibling.  E.g. a leaf (shift 0) with an order-1 entry at 0..1 and an
entry at 2: a walk from index 1 yields index 1 with xa_offset 0, and
xas_pause() sets xa_index = 1 + (2 - 0) = 3, skipping index 2.  Still
present in v7.1.  Fix: measure the step from xa_index's own slot
(get_offset()), after masking the bits under node->shift.
Applied by scripts/pin-worktree.sh (git apply) for the pin's fixed state.

--- a/lib/xarray.c
+++ b/lib/xarray.c
@@ -1152,7 +1152,8 @@
 			if (!xa_is_sibling(xa_entry(xas->xa, node, offset)))
 				break;
 		}
-		xas->xa_index += (offset - xas->xa_offset) << node->shift;
+		xas->xa_index &= ~0UL << node->shift;
+		xas->xa_index += (offset - get_offset(xas->xa_index, node)) << node->shift;
 		if (xas->xa_index == 0)
 			xas->xa_node = XAS_BOUNDS;
 	} else {
